# ---------------------------------------------------- SQ3 COLOCATION
CO-01|Software|squad:colocation|Sprint 0|task|P0|3|Scaffold the colocation service and seed rack inventory|Three synthetic sites with racks, power feeds and cooling capacity.
CO-02|Software|squad:colocation|Sprint 1|story|P0|5|View available rack space and power capacity by site|As an ops lead I can see what is free before I ask for it.
CO-03|Software|squad:colocation|Sprint 2|story|P0|5|Request a rack reservation with power and cooling requirements|Capture kW draw, redundancy needs and requested start date. Validate against remaining capacity.
CO-04|Software|squad:colocation|Sprint 2|story|P1|5|Raise and track a remote-hands ticket with a severity level|A P1 at 2am is the whole point. Include expected response time per severity.
CO-05|Software|squad:colocation|Sprint 3|story|P1|5|Show power draw per rack against the contracted limit|Chart actual against contracted, with a visual warning as the customer approaches the limit.
CO-06|Software|squad:colocation|Sprint 3|story|P2|3|Upload and store a site access request document|Store in MinIO with access control and a retention policy.
CO-07|Software|squad:colocation|Sprint 4|task|P1|3|Prevent double-booking of a rack under concurrent requests|Two customers reserving the same rack at once must not both succeed. Write the failing test first.
CO-08|Software|squad:colocation|Sprint 4|spike|P2|2|Decide how to model partial-rack unit-level reservations|Customers want 4U, not a whole rack. Timebox one day and write an ADR.
