# -------------------------------------------------------- SQ5 ENERGY
EN-01|Software|squad:energy|Sprint 0|task|P0|3|Scaffold the telemetry service and a synthetic meter generator|Generate realistic solar and battery curves including cloudy days and outages.
EN-02|Software|squad:energy|Sprint 1|story|P0|5|Ingest meter readings through an authenticated endpoint|Device authentication, schema validation, and rejection of readings from unknown meters.
EN-03|Software|squad:energy|Sprint 2|story|P0|5|Site dashboard showing solar generation and battery state of charge|As a site owner I can see at a glance whether my site is generating and how much runtime is left.
EN-04|Software|squad:energy|Sprint 2|story|P1|5|Time-series aggregation for hourly, daily and monthly views|Pre-aggregate so the dashboard stays fast as data grows. TimescaleDB is a reasonable starting point.
EN-05|Software|squad:energy|Sprint 3|story|P1|5|Alert when battery state of charge falls below a threshold|Configurable per site. Must not fire repeatedly for the same incident.
EN-06|Software|squad:energy|Sprint 3|spike|P2|3|Choose a time-series storage approach and justify it|Partitioned PostgreSQL against TimescaleDB against VictoriaMetrics. Write an ADR.
EN-07|Software|squad:energy|Sprint 4|task|P1|3|Backfill and gap handling for missing meter readings|Sites lose connectivity. Distinguish a real zero from a missing reading.
EN-08|Software|squad:energy|Sprint 4|story|P2|3|Export site energy data as CSV|Date-ranged export for the customer's own analysis.
